[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2152","id":4831739465,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT-9fds8AAAABH_5-SQ","html_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2152","diff_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2152.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2152.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2152","number":2152,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(pr): the read-back budget is a first read plus 3 retries (5s/15s/45s)","user":{"login":"hpo-author[bot]","id":331381602,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOE8B7Yg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70032254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/hpo-author","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Today's measured class (pre-study P2, 2026-10-12): app_push pushed successfully, then the read-back GET hit a transient GitHub failure (502 / empty response); the budget (6 flat 2s settles, ~12s) exhausted, app_push refused \"the pull request did not read back\", and the train stopped -- twice today, ~90s recovery each on relaunch, ≈1h20m of train time for the first instance alone. This change makes the read-back's existing retry loop distinguish TRANSPORT failures (the read could not be performed: HTTP 5xx, network error, timeout, unparseable/empty answer where a PR document was expected) from MISMATCHES (a completed read that differs from what was meant to be posted), and gives transport an exponential budget: RB_TRIES 6→4 (a first read plus 3 retries), RB_SLEEP 2→5, settling 5s/15s/45s (~65s of sleeps) -- enough to ride out the measured ~90s transient class without any relaunch. A mismatch never retries: `body` at the pushed sha and `bad state=...` refuse on the first read, exactly as before -- the byte-identical read-back (comment-readback.md) is the safety property and a retried mismatch would read as slow success. The `stale` race arm is untouched. Both refusal wordings are unchanged.\n\n## Head\n\n`dd2485d16bed643a00cb1226ed7d4473bb057cac` is the orchestrator's recarry of main into the previous head. It is not a clean merge of the live head and main (HEAD has 1 parent(s), not a 2-parent merge), so prepr checked this head.\n\n`dd2485d16bed643a00cb1226ed7d4473bb057cac` on `fix/readback-backoff`.\n\n## Mutation proof\n\n`tools/pr/app_push.sh --self-test`, new arms R9-TRANSPORT-RETRY. Reverting confirm_readback to the pre-fix semantics (flat `RB_SLEEP` settle, no `bad state=` refusal) while keeping the arms, 3 go red:\n\n- FAIL and the settles GROW: 1s then 3s (the exponential 5s/15s/45s shape at the injected scale) (got '20', want '11')\n- FAIL and the refusal names the real settle total, the geometric sum (got '0', want '1')\n- FAIL zero retries, zero settles: one read, no sleeping (got '32', want '10')\n\nArm (a) (502 on the first read, then the pushed PR → confirmed, no refusal) passes under flat logic at the injected 1s scale -- at the real defaults the flat budget was 6×2s ≈ 12s, which is precisely the exhaustion measured today; the growth checks above are what pin the exponential shape the ride-out depends on.\n\n## Null control\n\nThe mismatch arm is the null control for the retry: a stubbed body mismatch (`mangle-body`) refuses on the FIRST read -- `get-n`=1, settles=0, zero retries -- and a stubbed completed read answering `state=closed` likewise refuses at once with no sleep. Both hold on the fixed tree; the retry fires only on the `error` transport branch.\n\n## Figures\n\n- self-test tally before the change: `bash tools/pr/app_push.sh --self-test` at origin/main → `app_push self-test: 110 checks, 0 failed`\n- after: same command at HEAD → `app_push self-test: 124 checks, 0 failed`\n- `python3 tools/audit/seat/tmp_paths.py --check` → `tmp_paths: 0 refused, 0 stale allow entries at HEAD`\n\n## Red checks\n\nnone\n\n## Forward-carry\n\nnone\n\n## Friction\n\nR9-TRANSPORT-RETRY: cost: two train stops of ~90s recovery each today (~1h20m for the first instance, pre-study §P2) from a transport hiccup the read-back's own refusal could have ridden out; this PR is the countermeasure.\n\n","created_at":"2026-10-12T15:46:12Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T18:02:54Z","closed_at":"2026-10-13T18:02:51Z","merged_at":"2026-10-13T18:02:51Z","merge_commit_sha":"6cdf2667257d243873b356d012e51f91baff7eb1","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2152/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2152/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2152/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/statuses/dd2485d16bed643a00cb1226ed7d4473bb057cac","head":{"label":"tvofi:fix/readback-backoff","ref":"fix/readback-backoff","sha":"dd2485d16bed643a00cb1226ed7d4473bb057cac","user":{"login":"tvofi","id":70032254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMDMyMjU0","avatar_url":"https://